<h2>A diversified market led by feed-grade fish meal</h2>
<p>Japan is one of the more diversified markets in our verified trade data — fish meal (driven by Japan's aquaculture sector) leads, with sesame seeds, black pepper, maize and smaller seafood lines like squid/cuttlefish and shrimp also moving. This is a different profile from the staple-commodity-dominated South Asian or Gulf markets, reflecting Japan's role as both a food-processing and feed-mill buyer.</p>

<h2>Standards set independently, tested accordingly</h2>
<p>The single most important operating fact for this market: Japan sets and enforces its own Maximum Residue Limits and food-safety standards, separate from the EU or US systems. A product that clears European or American import testing is not automatically cleared for Japan. We test and document specifically against Japan's own limits for any Japan-bound order — tell us early if Japan is your destination so we can confirm the right testing panel before shipment, not after a rejection.</p>

<h2>Transit and payment</h2>
<p>Yokohama, Kobe and Nagoya are all realistic entry ports, with transit generally running 16-22 days depending on routing. Confirmed LC is typical for a first order with a new Japanese buyer, with established relationships often moving to TT.</p>

